  "FLINK-18726": {
    "jira_id": "FLINK-18726",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Fixed",
    "title": "Support INSERT INTO specific columns",
    "description": "Currently Flink only supports insert into a table without specifying columns, but most database systems support insert into specific columns by\r\n\r\n{code:sql}\r\nINSERT INTO table_name(column1, column2, ...) ...\r\n{code}\r\n\r\nThe columns not specified will be filled with default values or {{NULL}} if no default value is given when creating the table.\r\n\r\nAs Flink currently does not support default values when creating tables, we can fill the unspecified columns with {{NULL}} and throw exceptions if there are columns with {{NOT NULL}} constraints.",
    "commits": [
      {
        "sha": "555a06ff0a7ceee1b7b563bbe2961f295a723206",
        "message": "[FLINK-18726][table-planner-blink] Support INSERT INTO specific columns in blink planner",
