  "FLINK-26047": {
    "jira_id": "FLINK-26047",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Fixed",
    "title": "Support usrlib in HDFS for YARN application mode",
    "description": "In YARN Application mode, we currently support using user jar and lib jar from HDFS. For example, we can run commands like:\r\n{quote}./bin/flink run-application -t yarn-application \\\r\n\t-Dyarn.provided.lib.dirs=\"hdfs://myhdfs/my-remote-flink-dist-dir\" \\\r\n\thdfs://myhdfs/jars/my-application.jar{quote}\r\nFor {{usrlib}}, we currently only support local directory. I propose to add HDFS support for {{usrlib}} to work with CLASSPATH_INCLUDE_USER_JAR better. It can also benefit cases like using notebook to submit flink job.",
